<%# Asking for the confirmation link again. #575.

    This is the page a real person who never got the email lands on, so it is not optional:
    without it Rodauth's unstyled built-in renders inside this app's layout, and the one
    screen standing between somebody and their account would be the one screen that looks
    broken.

    It is reached three ways, which is why the form has to work when it is a page and when it
    is a response. Rodauth returns this view in place of the login form when an unconfirmed
    address tries to sign in (`verify_account.rb:275-282`) and in place of the sign-up form
    when an unconfirmed address signs up again (`verify_account.rb:189-196`), and it is also
    at /verify-account-resend on its own. In the first two cases the address has just been
    typed, so it is carried through as a hidden field rather than asked for twice; on its own
    the field is shown.

    The action and the CSRF token both name verify_account_resend_path explicitly. They have
    to: on the first two routes in this page is rendered at /login and /create-account, and
    Roda's csrf_tag binds a token to the path it is given, so a token minted for the current
    path would be refused by the post. That failure is a 403 on the one form a locked-out
    person is using.

    The copy says "if there is an account" rather than "we have sent you an email", the same
    way views/reset-password-request.erb does and for the same reason: app.rb answers this
    form identically for an address with no account, so the sentence has to stay true when
    nothing was sent. %>
<div class="flex min-h-full flex-col justify-center px-6 py-12 lg:px-8">
  <div class="sm:mx-auto sm:w-full sm:max-w-sm">
    <h1 class="text-center text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-gray-900">Confirm your address</h1>
    <%== render('_form_error') %>
    <p class="mt-4 text-center text-sm text-gray-600">
      This account is waiting on a link sent by email. Until the address is confirmed there is
      no way in, which is how an account nobody asked for stays shut.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-10 sm:mx-auto sm:w-full sm:max-w-sm">
    <form action="<%= rodauth.verify_account_resend_path %>" method="post" class="space-y-6" role="form"
          id="verify-account-resend-form" autocomplete="on">
      <%== rodauth.csrf_tag(rodauth.verify_account_resend_path) %>
      <% if rodauth.param_or_nil(rodauth.login_param) %>
        <%== rodauth.login_hidden_field %>
      <% else %>
        <div>
          <label for="email" class="block text-sm font-medium leading-6 text-gray-900">Email address</label>
          <div class="mt-2">
            <%# name="login" and autocomplete="email", matching the sign-in, sign-up and reset
                forms. A password manager offers back what it saved there only if every form
                names the identifier the same way. %>
            <input id="email" name="login" type="email" autocomplete="email" required
                   class="<%= field_style %> block w-full py-1.5 text-gray-900 placeholder:text-gray-400 sm:text-sm sm:leading-6">
          </div>
        </div>
      <% end %>
      <div>
        <button type="submit" class="<%= button_style %> flex w-full justify-center bg-lime-500 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-semibold leading-6 text-gray-900 hover:bg-lime-600">Send the link again</button>
      </div>
    </form>

    <p class="mt-10 text-center text-sm text-gray-500">
      Confirmed it already?
      <a href="/login" class="font-semibold leading-6 text-lime-700 hover:text-lime-800">Log in</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
